# Code owners are requested for review automatically. The point is not
# gatekeeping, it is that some parts of this repo are load-bearing for
# everything else and should not change without the person who will have to
# live with it seeing the change.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the specific entries below override the
# catch-all.

# Everything, unless something more specific claims it.
*                       @bradhe

# The contract crates define the vocabulary every other crate compiles
# against. Two people independently improving a shared trait is the failure
# mode this file exists to catch, and it is invisible until the merge.
/crates/orbita-core/    @bradhe
/crates/orbita-runtime/ @bradhe
/crates/orbita-objectstore/ @bradhe
/crates/orbita-proto/   @bradhe

# The wire protocol is a published interface. Changing it breaks clients that
# share no code with the server.
/proto/                 @bradhe

# The simulation harness is the basis of the correctness claim, so a change
# that weakens it is worse than a bug.
/crates/orbita-sim/     @bradhe

# Requirements and accepted decisions. Records are immutable once accepted; a
# change here should usually be a new record instead.
/docs/REQUIREMENTS.md   @bradhe
/docs/adr/              @bradhe

# Build, release, and deployment surface.
/.github/               @bradhe
/Dockerfile             @bradhe
/docker-compose.yml     @bradhe
/deploy/                @bradhe

# Project governance.
/LICENSE                @bradhe
/NOTICE                 @bradhe
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md     @bradhe
/SECURITY.md            @bradhe
